{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/glibobject\/typevaluecollectfunc"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"title":"TypeValueCollectFunc","externalID":"s:10GLibObject20TypeValueCollectFunca","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TypeValueCollectFunc"}],"symbolKind":"typealias","modules":[{"name":"GLibObject"}],"roleHeading":"Type Alias","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TypeValueCollectFunc"}]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"This function is responsible for converting the values collected from","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a variadic argument list into contents suitable for storage in a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/Value"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TypeValueCollectFunc","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" = ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GTypeValueCollectFunc","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@GTypeValueCollectFunc"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This function should setup "},{"code":"value","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" similar to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeValueInitFunc","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"; e.g.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for a string value that does not allow ","type":"text"},{"code":"NULL","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" pointers, it needs to either"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"emit an error, or do an implicit conversion by storing an empty string.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value"},{"type":"text","text":" passed in to this function has a zero-filled data array, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"just like for "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeValueInitFunc","type":"reference"},{"text":" it is guaranteed to not contain any old","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"contents that might need freeing.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nCollectValues"},{"type":"text","text":" argument is the string length of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collect_format"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"field of "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeValueTable"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"collect_values","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is an array of "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeCValue","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with length of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nCollectValues"},{"text":", containing the collected values according","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collect_format"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"collectFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" argument provided as a hint by the caller. It may","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"contain the flag "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/valueNocopyContents","isActive":true},{"text":" indicating that the collected","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value contents may be considered ‘static’ for the duration of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"lifetime. Thus an extra copy of the contents stored in ","type":"text"},{"code":"collectValues","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"not required for assignment to "},{"code":"value","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For our above string example, we continue with:","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"(C Language Example):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"C","code":["if (!collect_values[0].v_pointer)","  value->data[0].v_pointer = g_strdup (\"\");","else if (collect_flags & G_VALUE_NOCOPY_CONTENTS)","  {","    value->data[0].v_pointer = collect_values[0].v_pointer;","    \/\/ keep a flag for the value_free() implementation to not free this string","    value->data[1].v_uint = G_VALUE_NOCOPY_CONTENTS;","  }","else","  value->data[0].v_pointer = g_strdup (collect_values[0].v_pointer);","return NULL;"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It should be noted, that it is generally a bad idea to follow the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/valueNocopyContents","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" hint for reference counted types. Due to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"reentrancy requirements and reference count assertions performed","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"by the signal emission code, reference counts should always be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"incremented for reference counted contents stored in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"value->data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"array. To deviate from our string example for a moment, and taking","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a look at an exemplary implementation for ","type":"text"},{"code":"GTypeValueTable.collect_value()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GObject"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"(C Language Example):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"C","code":["GObject *object = G_OBJECT (collect_values[0].v_pointer);","g_return_val_if_fail (object != NULL,","   g_strdup_printf (\"Object %p passed as invalid NULL pointer\", object));","\/\/ never honour G_VALUE_NOCOPY_CONTENTS for ref-counted types","value->data[0].v_pointer = g_object_ref (object);","return NULL;"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The reference count for valid objects is always incremented, regardless"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of "},{"code":"collect_flags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". For invalid objects, the example returns a newly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"allocated string without altering ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Upon success, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collect_value()"},{"type":"text","text":" needs to return "},{"code":"NULL","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". If, however,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"an error condition occurred, "},{"code":"collect_value()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" should return a newly"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"allocated string containing an error diagnostic."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The calling code makes no assumptions about the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value"},{"type":"text","text":" contents being"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"valid upon error returns, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value"},{"text":" is simply thrown away without further","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"freeing. As such, it is a good idea to not allocate "},{"code":"GValue","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" contents"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prior to returning an error; however, "},{"code":"collect_values()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is not obliged","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to return a correctly setup ","type":"text"},{"code":"value","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for error returns, simply because","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any non-"},{"code":"NULL","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" return is considered a fatal programming error, and"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"further program behaviour is undefined."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeValueCollectFunc"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject"]]},"references":{"doc://GLibObject/documentation/GLibObject/TypeValueInitFunc":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TypeValueInitFunc","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeValueInitFunc","url":"\/documentation\/glibobject\/typevalueinitfunc","title":"TypeValueInitFunc","abstract":[{"text":"Initializes the value contents by setting the fields of the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value->data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TypeValueInitFunc","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GLibObject/documentation/GLibObject/Value":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This class is the main Swift wrapper with memory management"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for underlying "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GValues"},{"type":"text","text":" (the opaque GLib structure used to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"hold different types of values.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/Value","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Value","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Value","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Value"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glibobject\/value"},"doc://GLibObject/documentation/GLibObject":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glibobject","title":"GLibObject","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GLibObject/documentation/GLibObject/TypeValueTable":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/glibobject\/typevaluetable","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TypeValueTable"}],"title":"TypeValueTable","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeValueTable","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TypeValueTable"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GLibObject/documentation/GLibObject/TypeValueCollectFunc":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TypeValueCollectFunc"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"TypeValueCollectFunc","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/glibobject\/typevaluecollectfunc","title":"TypeValueCollectFunc","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This function is responsible for converting the values collected from"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a variadic argument list into contents suitable for storage in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/Value"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLibObject\/documentation\/GLibObject\/TypeValueCollectFunc"},"doc:/